# Build output. OWNERSHIP's `ignored:` list has said both of these were
# gitignored since the split, in a repository that had no .gitignore at all
# (A418) — so `git add -A` after a goreleaser run was one command away from
# committing a dist/ full of release archives.
#
# Every pattern is anchored, and the binaries have to be. An unanchored
# `ferry` matches any path component of that name, which includes cmd/ferry/,
# so it would silently ignore new files in the package that builds the
# binary. `gitignore_test.go` measures that.

# goreleaser's output (.goreleaser.yaml, U6).
/dist/

# The binary a local `go build` drops in the module root.
/ferry

# The faultinject build, which e2e/run.sh names and a local run may too.
/ferry-fault

# Git worktrees. Skipped by the ownership lint too — see worktreeDir in
# ownership_test.go for why a nested checkout is not a path OWNERSHIP can own.
/.worktrees/
